#exception-box(title: "THE SEVEN FATAL CUET TRAPS")[
  1. *Trap 1 (First General Election Year):* The election spanned from *October 1951 to February 1952*; it is officially referred to as the *1952 Election*.
  2. *Trap 2 (First Chief Election Commissioner):* The first CEC was *Sukumar Sen*, NOT T.N. Seshan or K.V.K. Sundaram.
  3. *Trap 3 (Kerala 1957 Election Result):* CPI formed the government under *E.M.S. Namboodiripad in 1957*, NOT in 1952; dismissed in *1959 under Article 356*.
  4. *Trap 4 (Congress System Author):* The term 'Congress System' was coined by political scientist *Rajni Kothari*, NOT Morris-Jones or Paul Brass.
  5. *Trap 5 (Swatantra Party Founding Trigger):* Swatantra Party was formed in *August 1959* in response to the *1959 Nagpur Resolution* on cooperative joint farming.
  6. *Trap 6 (CPI Split Year):* The Communist Party split into CPI and CPI(M) in *1964* following the Sino-Soviet rift and 1962 war, NOT in 1957 or 1969.
  7. *Trap 7 (Integral Humanism Philosopher):* Integral Humanism was propounded by *Pandit Deendayal Upadhyaya*, NOT Shyama Prasad Mukherjee or Veer Savarkar.
]

